cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "teakit: techno-economic analysis of chemical process plants"
message: "If you use teakit in published work, please cite the article under preferred-citation, and cite the underlying DOE/NETL and NREL sources it implements."
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-18
license-url: "https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free Python library and graphical application for the
  techno-economic analysis of chemical process plants. Implements the DOE/NETL
  capital cost cascade (BEC to TASC), 42 equipment cost correlations regressed
  from DOE/NETL-2002/1169 Appendix B, CEPCI escalation, factored operating cost
  models, byproduct allocation, three levelised-cost methods including an
  after-tax discounted cash flow solved for minimum selling price, and
  sensitivity analysis by tornado, sweep, Monte Carlo and breakeven.
keywords:
  - techno-economic analysis
  - process economics
  - cost estimation
  - chemical engineering
  - levelized cost
  - discounted cash flow
repository-code: "https://github.com/alotfi73/teakit"
url: "https://github.com/alotfi73/teakit"
